$Aeon::Books["Skill_Aggr_z","cntnt"] = "So you want to become a Farmer? This is the skill of <f2>Aggriculture<f1>, or growing crops. Aggriculture is a vital skill, that has heavily impacted history, altering nations power and self-sufficiency, however, that is a topic of debate, left for another discussion at a later time. Now, the first step to Aggriculture will be obtaining a <f2>Seed<f1>. You can purchase Seeds from the <f2>Central Market<f1> at one of the <f2>Terminals<f1>. Before you can become Farmer John, you must first obtain a piece of <f2>Real Estate<f1> or kindly ask a Neighbor for <f2>Permission<f1> to plant seeds on their land! Once you have found a suitable location to start your crop, select the Seed from your <f2>Inventory<f1> and click <f2>Use<f1> to attempt to plant it where you are looking, within a short range. <f3>Harvesting the Crop:<f1> Once a plant has become ripe, one may notice a '<f2>Ripe-Spark<f1>' fire from the top of it, indicating that it can be harvested! To harvest your crop, simply use your <f2>Construction Tool<f1> and uproot the Plant... once you release it you can collect it like any other object. After a Plant becomes Ripe, it will also begin to <f2>Seed<f1>, and produce more Plants to Harvest, so patience may be a virtue in Aggriculture! One of the basics of learning Aggriculture, is learning how to properly <f2>Fertilize<f1> Plants, and the more you know about Aggriculture, the better you can Fertilize Plants! You can do so by binding the Aggriculture <f2>Skill Func<f1> to a key, if you don't know how, please refer to the Book '<f2>Key Binding<f1>'. That concludes the Introduction to Aggriculture! Please make sure you return this book before you are charged with a late fee!";
